lifeos-nix patch f4-a — Neutralize the self-update egress path

PROBLEM
  `LIFEOS/TOOLS/lifeos.ts` (the launcher this Nix build execs) ships a self-update
  path that phones out to two hosts the moment a user runs `k update` / `k version`:
    - getLatestVersion() → GET https://storage.googleapis.com/claude-code-dist-.../latest
    - cmdUpdate()        → `brew upgrade bun` + `curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash`
  On a Nix-packaged install this is both wrong (Claude Code + the LifeOS payload are
  pinned by store hash — you cannot self-update a read-only /nix/store path) and a
  default-reachable egress surface that violates the point-1 privacy invariant
  (default background egress ⊆ {Anthropic}).

FIX (surgical, 2 hunks, one file)
  - getLatestVersion(): return null before any fetch. The storage.googleapis.com probe
    is removed outright; `cmdVersion()` still prints "Current: vX" and simply omits the
    "Latest:" line (it already guards on a null latest).
  - cmdUpdate(): drop the `brew upgrade` and the `curl claude.ai/install.sh | bash`
    steps; print a Nix-aware message telling the user updates come from bumping the
    lifeos-nix flake input and rebuilding. getCurrentVersion() (local, no egress) kept.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  Touches only two functions in LIFEOS/TOOLS/lifeos.ts. Disjoint from f4-b (ElevenLabs,
  different files) and from f2 (DeployCore.ts). No other call sites of getLatestVersion.

VERIFICATION
  `rg 'storage\.googleapis\.com|claude\.ai/install\.sh|brew (upgrade|install)'` over the
  patched file returns no code (comments only). Hunks generated via `diff -u`, never
  hand-counted (lesson from patch 0005).

